WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.730
A fish takes its oxygen from water.

2
00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:04.980
You take yours from air.

3
00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:09.850
Water is the harder source: it
holds far less oxygen than air does.

4
00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:15.000
A leaf has neither gills nor lungs,
yet it swaps gases with the air too.

5
00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:19.370
Three very different organs,
all doing the same job well.

6
00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:22.960
So what do lungs, gills
and leaves have in common?

7
00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:27.060
In this mission, you'll build the checklist
that every efficient exchange surface

8
00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:27.940
meets.

9
00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:32.310
Then you'll put that checklist to work
on surfaces you have never met before,

10
00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:34.480
and predict how they must be built.

11
00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:39.630
Your mission: find out what makes lungs,
gills and leaves so good at swapping

12
00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:40.360
gases.
